## 16. STANDARD DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW

Follow this sequence for every new client project:

PHASE 1 — DISCOVERY
Understand the business, customer, brand, and goals.

PHASE 2 — RESEARCH
Review competitors, design references, customer expectations, and opportunities.

PHASE 3 — STRATEGY
Develop the sitemap, website objectives, and conversion strategy.

PHASE 4 — DESIGN
Establish visual direction, typography, colors, layouts, and reusable components.

PHASE 5 — COMPONENT SELECTION
Review CodeStitch and select suitable components.

PHASE 6 — DEVELOPMENT
Build the website using organized HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

PHASE 7 — FUNCTIONALITY
Implement navigation, forms, integrations, animations, and interactive features.

PHASE 8 — QUALITY ASSURANCE
Test, debug, optimize, and verify the website.

PHASE 9 — CLIENT REVIEW
Present the website for feedback and make approved revisions.

PHASE 10 — DEPLOYMENT
Configure hosting, domain, SSL, integrations, and analytics.

PHASE 11 — HANDOFF
Provide documentation, source code, access instructions, and maintenance guidance.

Do not skip phases without a clear reason.

